From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 14:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: reset recovery bookkeeping when the device
 stops

A recovery requested while mac80211 is suspending can never complete:
ieee80211_restart_hw() is not serviced across a system suspend, so
ath10k_stop() tears the device down with pending_recovery still set.
Every recovery request on a later cycle then times out against the
stale pending flag and increments fail_cont_count, and after
ATH10K_RECOVERY_MAX_FAIL_COUNT such cycles the driver declares itself
WEDGED mid-suspend, rerouting the teardown through paths slow enough
to trip the DPM watchdog. Measured on a WCN3990 phone that suspends
with the interface associated: the sixth WiFi suspend after boot
wedged the SoC, deterministically, five clean cycles then death.

The device is down and the next start boots fresh firmware; start the
recovery bookkeeping fresh too.
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
index 988a3a9bfc6c..195f46fc996f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/mac.c
@@ -5436,6 +5436,17 @@ static void ath10k_stop(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, bool suspend)
 			}
 		}
 		ar->state = ATH10K_STATE_OFF;
+
+		/* A recovery abandoned by this stop can never complete:
+		 * mac80211 does not service ieee80211_restart_hw() across a
+		 * suspend, so a stale pending_recovery would make every
+		 * later recovery request count as a consecutive failure
+		 * until ATH10K_RECOVERY_MAX_FAIL_COUNT wedges the driver.
+		 * The device is down and the next start boots fresh
+		 * firmware; start its recovery bookkeeping fresh too.
+		 */
+		atomic_set(&ar->pending_recovery, 0);
+		atomic_set(&ar->fail_cont_count, 0);
 	}
 	mutex_unlock(&ar->conf_mutex);
 
